## INTRO & INFO
== ============
this text document acts as a general reference to
the rzk instruction set architecture, alongside
references on its first implementation, rz1600,
in which is emulated through the er1600 program.

## REGISTERS
== =========
the rzk instruction set architecture uses nine
hardware registers. the following are listed:

   A B C & D: general-purpose sixteen-bit
   registers.
   
   F: eight-bit flags register
   
   J & K: twenty-four-bit pointer registers.
   
   P: twenty-four-bit instruction pointer.
   Q: twenty-four-bit stack pointer.
   
## INSTRUCTIONS
== ============   
the rzk instruction set architecture has a total
of sixty-four instructions. an instruction is a
single byte containing two bit fields:

[011001][00]

the first bit field, "I", contains six bits. it
is also known as the "instruction field", and
determines the instruction being executed. the
second bit field, "S", contains two bits. it is
also known as the "selection field", and acts as
a modifier to the instruction being executed.